WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.650
This is Lattis, a spreadsheet where
every table is also a real database.

2
00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:08.925
You type your data as usual.

3
00:00:08.975 --> 00:00:14.200
Lattis recognizes the table and
turns it into a real SQL table.

4
00:00:16.233 --> 00:00:18.733
And the sheet has no size limit.

5
00:00:20.688 --> 00:00:23.613
Formulas use the names of your columns,

6
00:00:24.421 --> 00:00:28.971
and look up a value in another
table, with no risk of misalignment.

7
00:00:30.971 --> 00:00:33.271
A pivot table, a chart;

8
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:42.950
a formula placed next to a pivot table
becomes a calculated column that follows it.

9
00:00:43.441 --> 00:00:45.891
And everything follows your data.

10
00:00:48.594 --> 00:00:49.819
Want to go further?

11
00:00:49.869 --> 00:00:53.219
The SQL tab queries your tables by name.

12
00:00:57.528 --> 00:01:00.203
And to automate, there are Lua scripts.

13
00:01:02.028 --> 00:01:03.903
Is your data somewhere else?

14
00:01:03.953 --> 00:01:07.303
Lattis connects to your
databases and your APIs,

15
00:01:07.353 --> 00:01:10.753
and replays your cleanup
steps on every refresh.

16
00:01:18.862 --> 00:01:22.437
It can also plug into your
AI tools, if you wish.

17
00:01:24.596 --> 00:01:27.571
On your own, everything
fits in a single file.

18
00:01:27.621 --> 00:01:32.721
As a team, there is Lattis Server, which
anyone can host wherever they like.

19
00:01:34.683 --> 00:01:38.208
It shares your workbooks with
permissions for each table,

20
00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:46.527
and you work online from the app,
or from a simple web browser,

21
00:01:46.577 --> 00:01:48.652
with nothing to install.

22
00:01:52.168 --> 00:01:56.393
And on a server, a table can also
become a form to fill in online:

23
00:01:56.443 --> 00:01:59.218
each answer arrives as a new row.

24
00:02:07.457 --> 00:02:11.107
Lattis is free and open
source: its code is public,

25
00:02:11.157 --> 00:02:13.807
so anyone can read it and improve it.

26
00:02:14.291 --> 00:02:16.641
It comes in five languages,

27
00:02:17.128 --> 00:02:19.978
on Windows, macOS and Linux.

28
00:02:20.462 --> 00:02:23.237
Lattis gives you the
flexibility of a spreadsheet,

29
00:02:23.287 --> 00:02:25.637
with the power of a database.
